Brute Force Approach:

class Solution {
    public void moveZeroes(int[] nums) {
        int []ans=new int[nums.length];
        int index=0;
        for(int i=0;i<nums.length;i++){
            if(nums[i]!=0){
                ans[index]=nums[i];
                index++;
            }
        }
        for(int i=0;i<nums.length;i++){
            nums[i]=ans[i];
        }
    }
}

Time  : O(n)
Space : O(n)

Optimal Approach:

class Solution {
    public void moveZeroes(int[] nums) {
       int left=0;
       for(int right=0;right<nums.length;right++){
            if(nums[right]!=0){
                int temp=nums[right];
                nums[right]=nums[left];
                nums[left]=temp;
                left++;
            }
       }
    }
}

At any point during the loop:

[ non-zero elements | elements not processed yet ]
                    ↑
                   left

Everything before left is already in the correct non-zero order.
right is exploring the remaining elements.
When right finds a non-zero:
nums[right] != 0
we put it at:
nums[left]
and advance left.

Time  : O(n)
Space : O(1)

